//? Title: VGG: Small Kernels, Depth and a Sliding Classifier
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Image recognition needs large spatial context without making every convolution kernel large.
VGG stacks small filters to increase receptive fields and nonlinear depth. We check all three
A/D/E depth schedules, show exactly how dense classifier weights become sliding convolutions,
and expose compact tensor Adam fits on original CIFAR-10 inputs.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.2_classic_architectures/vgg.cpp`.

> The method

Configurations A/D/E have convolution counts (1,1,2,2,2), (2,2,3,3,3), and (2,2,4,4,4).
Five 2×2 stride-two pools follow blocks with widths 64/128/256/512/512; three dense layers
complete depths 11/16/19. There is no BN or LRN. ReLU follows every hidden layer and dropout
applies to the two hidden dense outputs. Two 3×3 convolutions have a 5×5 receptive box:

$$
\text{weights}(3\times3\to3\times3)=18C^2<25C^2=
\text{weights}(5\times5),\qquad r_{two}=1+2+2=5.
$$
\alttext(At equal input/intermediate/output widths, two three-by-three kernels use eighteen C squared weights versus twenty-five C squared for one five-by-five filter.)

The comparison assumes equal widths and excludes biases; extra ReLUs make the function classes
different. The learned feature map for a 224-pixel image is 7×7. FC6 can be reshaped into a
7×7 VALID kernel, with FC7/8 becoming 1×1 kernels. Their inference outputs agree on each feature
window. This does not imply equality to separately cropped raw images, where context and
padding can differ. Conv work is O(NHW k² Cin Cout), and the reference dense head can dominate
parameter memory. The report checks compact stage layouts and uses the original full-model
counts only as separately computed shape arithmetic, without allocating all full-size weights.

For three visible Adam fits, keep every block/depth but use 32-pixel inputs, width divisor
eight and dense width 32, with He initialization and [-1,1] input scaling. Fit 128 rows,
validate on the next 64 and evaluate 64 official test rows after thirty epochs. These CPU
subset demonstrations are not full-width ImageNet results or an architecture ranking.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/vgg_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/vgg_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/vgg_concept.tikz > build/vgg_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/vgg_concept.svg build/vgg_concept.dvi > build/vgg_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
