> Interpreting the short fit

The selected training NLLs remain around 1.9–2.3, and held-out accuracy is near or below
chance on these tiny subsets. The runs check the visible optimisation/checkpoint workflow;
they do not demonstrate successful large-data training or rank the three depths. The
separate architecture and sliding-head identities remain valid regardless of these fit scores.

> Native confusion matrices

These matrices use the held-out predictions from the executed program above.
The native `ConfusionMatrix` SVG API labels exact counts with true classes
running from top to bottom and predicted classes from left to right.

