> Conclusion

All A/D/E schedules retain their named depths and five pooling stages. Dense and sliding
convolutional heads agree on matching feature windows. Compact explicit Adam fits illustrate
training and checkpoint selection; their small fixed subsets do not establish a depth ranking.

> References

- [Simonyan and Zisserman (2015), Very Deep Convolutional Networks for Large-Scale Image Recognition](https://arxiv.org/abs/1409.1556).
- [CIFAR-10 binary dataset](https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html).
